---
code: lint-tool-failed-without-findings
when-fires: an external linter exited nonzero but produced nothing parseable. lint/source_external.rs. `{tool}` is the tool, `{rc}` its exit status.
why: 27R §8 delta-exit-trichotomy-sharpened - the adapter never interprets a foreign tool-rc beyond zero/nonzero (checkbashisms' additive 1|2|4 codes are the named trap), so an unexplained failure is reported as itself. Replay injects a raw process outcome through the lint runner edge.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
true

-- edge-fault --
tool-run shellcheck 2

-- replay --
$ dorc lint book.sh
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

book.sh:
  - warn [shellcheck:lint-tool-failed-without-findings] `shellcheck` exited with status 2 without producing any findings Dorc could read, so its checks contributed nothing here -- run it directly to see its own report. (raw)

dorc lint: 0 errors, 1 warning, 0 infos across 1 file.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-tool-failed-without-findings
{{tool}} = "shellcheck"
{{rc}} = "2"
{{v0}} = "0"
{{v1}} = "s"
{{v2}} = "1"
{{v3}} = ""
{{v4}} = "0"
{{v5}} = "s"
{{v6}} = "1"
{{v7}} = ""
